.SS " bool pip\&._internal\&.metadata\&.base\&.BaseDistribution\&.installed_by_distutils ( self)"

.PP
.nf
Whether this distribution is installed with legacy distutils format\&.

A distribution installed with 'raw' distutils not patched by setuptools
uses one single file at ``info_location`` to store metadata\&. We need to
treat this specially on uninstallation\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.PP
Reimplemented in \fBpip\&._internal\&.metadata\&.pkg_resources\&.Distribution\fP\&.
.SS " Optional[str] pip\&._internal\&.metadata\&.base\&.BaseDistribution\&.installed_location ( self)"

.PP
.nf
The distribution's 'installed' location\&.

This should generally be a ``site-packages`` directory\&. This is
usually ``dist\&.location``, except for legacy develop-installed packages,
where ``dist\&.location`` is the source code location, and this is where
the ``\&.egg-link`` file is\&.

The returned location is normalized (in particular, with symlinks removed)\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.PP
Reimplemented in \fBpip\&._internal\&.metadata\&.importlib\&._dists\&.Distribution\fP, and \fBpip\&._internal\&.metadata\&.pkg_resources\&.Distribution\fP\&.
.SS " bool pip\&._internal\&.metadata\&.base\&.BaseDistribution\&.installed_with_dist_info ( self)"

.PP
.nf
Whether this distribution is installed with the 'modern format'\&.

This indicates a 'modern' installation, e\&.g\&. storing metadata in the
``\&.dist-info`` directory\&. This applies to installations made by
setuptools (but through pip, not directly), or anything using the
standardized build backend interface (PEP 517)\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " bool pip\&._internal\&.metadata\&.base\&.BaseDistribution\&.installed_with_setuptools_egg_info ( self)"

.PP
.nf
Whether this distribution is installed with the ``\&.egg-info`` format\&.

This usually indicates the distribution was installed with setuptools
with an old pip version or with ``single-version-externally-managed``\&.

Note that this ensure the metadata store is a directory\&. distutils can
also installs an ``\&.egg-info``, but as a file, not a directory\&. This
property is *False* for that case\&. Also see ``installed_by_distutils``\&.

.fi
.PP
 
